    "body": "The shared prototype census found protected entry gains that worsened the fixed objective. This change executes its declared single compensation: token 617, lane 0, code 58 → 48, followed by one fresh shared Generate coefficient gradient and one adjacent-Q4 construction. It preserves the original 84 winners plus the gained entry as 85 constraints, while retaining the same 588-term objective and all declared frozen families.\n\nThe selected composite lowers combined native CE from **8.52634374894637 to 8.216818642455662**, beating the original baseline rather than merely improving the worse prototype intermediate (8.634086267334682). It accepts 2,930 coefficient changes; 55,630 coordinates are saturated and none is rejected. All 85 complete pools survive independent export/reload.\n\nActual autoregressive correct entries improve **8 → 10**, while complete replies remain **8/512**, with all eight originals retained and no complete gains or losses. There are 201 changed output sequences; `useful_candidate=false`. The original accepted model remains accepted. Newly reached input 399 emits 617, then 3817 instead of 2097. Matched successful cases have the same prefix and query/prefix encoding state but different bank-conditioned Generate states. The next dependency is target-free bank/bridge/factor capture before another learning rule.\n\nAttempt 1 failed before gradient or construction because a nested checkpoint lacked its authenticated plans. The sealed failure is preserved. The repair copies exact root plan bytes and checks complete child reference bindings in both checkpoint paths, with a regression test. It changes no experiment rule. Attempt 2 completed and sealed 1,240 files.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Executed source `08c477ebdf5d1e4f70c5c2b1c7b882e606f20a6d`: formatting, 46 fitter tests, two CPU/CUDA coefficient-credit parity tests and release build pass. Mathematical, adversarial and execution-boundary reviews pass.\n- Independent saved-evidence endpoint checks pass for 1,024 original/final outputs, 85 pools and 58,560 trials. Seven actual Rust complete-file BLAKE3 seal checks, decision analysis and six authenticated prior-output comparisons pass. No forward/backward or greedy-solver replication is claimed.\n- Final exact head `23511b8db63559732d1b7bf3f05da5e80ccf7f76`: adversarial review, formatting, all 46 fitter tests, both parity tests and release build pass with zero failures or ignored tests. Only the evidence documents differ from executed source. Compatibility CI acknowledgements are separate from these actual checks.\n\nPrivate preserved runtime: `3ffd50e24f112284ee273ae84c8d7f9c598420d2`. Complete audited result: `571ce48fa852df2957e8bc31573ec36b40291d15`, archive SHA256 `bbc0204f333647de16ef596e6de7e5a149baa98411055a48f3d6d1a71fbd3ca5` (108,122,616 bytes). Failed attempt: `627b8901caa2a69273bf817b24994d7c06361c8e`. Every publication was freshly downloaded and hash-verified. Source-linked details and cumulative costs are in `docs/evidence/native-prototype-compensation-2026-10-08.json` and current state.\n\nThis is exposed development optimization and entry learning. It does not qualify held-out transfer, useful conversation, general prose, geometric advantage or complete-path D11 energy savings. The persistent goal remains active. References #820.\n",
